# /home/deploy/.ssh/authorized_keys (deploy:deploy 0600), one line.
# "restrict" turns off port/agent/X11 forwarding and the terminal; "command"
# replaces whatever the client asks to run. The client's text (the tag)
# arrives as $SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND and is passed as one argument; the
# script and the sudoers rule both validate it.
restrict,command="sudo -n /usr/local/sbin/rmx-deploy-probe \"$SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND\"" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...public-key... rmx-backend-probe-deploy
